nity.com/profiles/76561198116490574/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 29, "playtime_forever": 13483, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6065, "last_played": 1788137026, "avatar": "62651e26f274aa56601155a5bab8bd3adefb6135"}, "language": "english", "review": "I really liked this game and I've been playing pretty regularly. I appreciate the different builds and the different ways scrolls and ascensions interact with each other, and of course the gunplay is pretty solid. I was afraid it would be too simple at first, but once you clear the first difficulty level, there's a bit more complexity courtesy of enemy modifiers and traps, and you're unlocking new weapons and scrolls and such.\n\nAs it is a rogue-lite, there's always the possibility of a string of bad drops that don't play well with your character or the build you're going for, and that's always frustrating. I've also found that on higher difficulty levels, it's really easy to get caught by surprise and one-shotted, especially if you haven't come across the scrolls you need to improve your survivability. Suicide bombers jumping out from around a corner, for example. Naturally, that'll happen more often at the beginning of a run.\n\nI've just gotten the last of the talents unlocked, and I'm trying to run through the reincarnation difficulty levels now. I might take a break to hunt some of the achievements stock up on those little green things. \n\nI'm looking forward to new content in the next update.", "timestamp_created": 1636234475, "timestamp_updated": 1636234475, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1637202540", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "102343889", "author": {"steamid": "76561198176201302", "personaname": "Tism Timmy", "persona_status": "offline", "profi